.TH CSTR_DESTROY 3 "2026-09-28" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
cstr_destroy \- destroy a cstr and set it to NULL
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cstring.h>

cstr_destroy(s);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This macro is the type-inferred form of cstring_destroy(). It destroys
the string and then sets the pointer to NULL.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
s   cstr lvalue to destroy, such as a variable or an element of an
    array; the macro evaluates it exactly once and sets it to NULL
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Calling it with a NULL pointer is safe and does nothing
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cstring_destroy (3)
